r family\nran: facts: reported in 91s; sota: reported in 42s; design: reported in 88s\nplan check: PASS \u2014 sota pinned on the door's token `sonnet` (the door refuses the full id; a first launch with the full id never started). All five points covered; point 1's \"15 of 22 sessions\" refusal count was not re-measured.\n\nFindings (no blocking finding: no factual error the recommendation depends on; P0 first holds):\n- facts \u00b7 verifiable \u00b7 memo:34 and :256: \"deleted after 180 days; nothing older than 2026-06 survives\" misattributes the June floor. Oldest padme transcript is 2026-06-10; 180 days back is 2026-05-04; repo history starts 2026-04-01. A shorter, earlier sweep (the 30-day default before settings.shared.json carried 180, first seen 6193cb37, 2026-07-22) fits. The P0 urgency date \"end of November\" should be about 2026-12-07. scenario: P0 is scheduled against the wrong date and the June floor's cause is misread (it also bears on the 2.3 headless-cleanup question). on main: n/a.\n- design \u00b7 verifiable \u00b7 memo:180: (file, line, tool_use_id) plus seekable zstd frames does not give access by line: a line number maps to no byte offset or frame without a line-to-frame map, which the design lacks; the survey (sota.md:47-50, 56) itself keeps whole-file decompression as the fallback. Store a byte offset or line-to-frame checkpoints, or accept whole-file decompression; age encryption needs the same plan. Raised independently by sota. scenario: a reader asking for a span near the end of a large cold transcript scans the whole file. on main: n/a.\n- design \u00b7 consider \u00b7 memo:133: \"closed = mtime older than one day\" plus an append-only archive leaves resumed sessions undefined (later appends, interrupted copies, which generation a pointer names). Add a resume-and-rearchive case to P0; its 3 h / 90 % excludes it.\n- design \u00b7 consider \u00b7 memo:157: dropping launch records where OTel links parentage needs the collector output in L0