: a87e43f9566ff173ef5ad9915cece772246bcd8b\nintent: verify the second, short revision of the monitoring memo keeps every must-have of the author's original ask intact: (a) no online refusal / friction removed, (b) durable transcripts for all runtimes including headless seats (vibe, aider, manuscript-review, claude -p, codex exec, pi), (c) execution flow with timings and costs of subagent and test calls sufficient for timeline bars, (d) pointers back into transcript spans, (e) an index addable later without data loss; check that each deferred item in \u00a7 5 really is optional and that nothing deferred is a must-have in disguise, and that the step costs and dependencies hold; include a seat from another model family, because this revision cut scope after the first panel and the author asked for an integrity re-review before a raid\nreview plan: two seats; mustheads (self, anthropic) traces (a)-(e) to the steps and checks the memo's door claims against routes.json, gaze_seat.py, seat_clock.py, manuscript_review.py, runtime_session.py; integrity (gpt-6.1-sol headless codex, openai) independent read of must-haves, deferrals, costs; budget 12m \u2014 the two seats converged on the same two gaps independently\nran: mustheads: reported in 95s; integrity: reported in 106s\nplan check: PASS \u2014 no deviation; all five must-haves, \u00a7 5 and \u00a7 6 covered. touched-tests: selected: none, result: skipped (no source or test file changed).\n\nFindings. (a) and (e) hold. (b), (c) and (d) have gaps the cut introduced or kept, each cheap to fix in the memo before the raid:\n- mustheads + integrity \u00b7 blocking (must-have b) \u00b7 memo:39, :130-132, :187: Pi headless seats run `pi --no-session -p` (skills/route/routes.json:104), and Pi's subagent extension spawns `pi ... --no-session` (routes.json:100). Neither writes a transcript, yet the memo lists Pi as \"kept\" and closes only three holes. Aider's seat rails also send chat, LLM and input history to /dev/null (routes.json:140), so a \"persistent home\" alone saves nothing. scenario: after step 2, a gaze run with a pi or aider seat leaves no transcript to archive, and step 2's exit still passes. on main: n/a. Fix: step 2 changes the pi door, the pi subagent extension and the aider rails so they write into the spool, and its exit checks newly generated transcripts per door.\n- mustheads + integrity \u00b7 blocking (must-have c) \u00b7 memo:141, :149-151: \"seat_clock.py run, which already launches every headless seat\" is false. skills/manuscript-review/manuscript_review.py:462,475 launches `claude -p` through its own Popen. `runtime.py session id` exports no id for Pi (scripts/runtime_session.py:5-6, ID_KEYS claude/codex only, verified). A child whose session cannot be pinned is left for \"a later join\" by start time that no step owns. Gaze launches seats of the same runtime concurrently in the same review-tree cwd, so that join is ambiguous. scenario: a manuscript-review run, a Pi-parent gaze or two concurrent codex seats produce no attachable or no unique lanes. Step 3's exit tests one gaze run only, so it passes. on main: n/a. Fix: step 3 covers manuscript_review (shared launch-line writer), names a Pi parent id (or records its absence), and records the child id the launcher can see (codex exec prints its session id on its captured output).\n- integrity \u00b7 verifiable \u00b7 memo:187-189: the exits can pass on Claude-only evidence. None requires each door, Codex/Pi subagents, test-call bars, shadow cost or pointer resolution. Add a small per-door coverage matrix to the step 2 and step 4 exits.\n- integrity + mustheads \u00b7 consider (the seat said blocking; downgraded after check) \u00b7 memo:159, :172: the pointer is named `(file, tool_use_id)`, but Codex uses `call_id` (scripts/tmp_report.py:355-359) and Pi uses `id`/`toolCallId` (scripts/trace-friction.py:425-438). Every runtime has a native id, so this is a naming and normalization line in `trace_events.py`, not a lost must-have. Aider's markdown history has no call id, so its pointer is file-level only; say so.\n- mustheads \u00b7 consider \u00b7 memo:159, :189: \"shadow USD\" needs a price table (Claude Code and Codex record tokens only; Codex counts are cumulative). Name its source in step 4.\n- mustheads + integrity \u00b7 consider \u00b7 memo:187, :191: reprice after adding the work above. Step 2 at 3-4 h / 75 % and step 3 at about 2 h are closer to the mark, for a total of about 9-12 h. The ordering holds: 1, 2 and 3 are independent, and 4 needs 2 and 3 once they own the full capture and linkage.\nDeferrals (\u00a7 5): span index, reader migration, OTel, seekable compression and encryption are genuinely optional, because the raw archive keeps what an index needs (e). The one deferral hiding a must-have is in row 4: the child-session and launcher identification noted above belongs in step 3, not deferred. The hook-based capture and the `Session:` trailer stay optional.\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: about 6m\ntelemetry: wall=na agents=1 tokens=na cost~=$na\nseat: mustheads \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=self \u00b7 model=anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 \u00b7 status: ran\nseat: integrity \u00b7 runtime=codex \u00b7 family=openai \u00b7 route=gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 model=openai/gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 status: ran\n"}

